      "body": "33 words for working life: the people (boss, manager, colleague, employee, staff), the places (company, factory, department, workplace), the paper and the money (application, contract, salary, wage), and what you do with them (apply, earn, employ).\nWatch the two prepositions: you work FOR a company or an employer, but you work IN a department, a factory, an industry.",
      "body_cz": "Pozor na předložky: work for a company, ale work in a department."
    },
    {
      "title": "You will use these words in",
      "frames": [
        "I am a …",
        "He is my …",
        "I work for …",
        "I work in …",
        "I have a …"
      ],
      "note": "employer and employee are one ending apart and mean opposite things: the employer pays, the employee is paid.",
      "note_cz": "employer = zaměstnavatel, employee = zaměstnanec. Liší se jen koncovkou."
    }
  ],
